\code{reason}: \code{"not_estimable"} (fewer than two sampling times with a positive
value, or a nonlinear fit that did not converge), \code{"no_decline"} (the
fitted \eqn{k} is not positive, so there is no DT50) and
\code{"no_uncertainty"} (no residual degrees of freedom, so no intervals).
